// Project-specific Biome (GritQL) lint plugin — white-labelling regression guard.
//
// Admins can rename model providers through the "Page settings" dialog, and the
// resolution lives in exactly one place per side: `shared/integration-overrides.ts`
// for the rules, and `useModelProviderCatalog` in
// `frontend/src/lib/integration-overrides.ts` for consumption.
//
// Only providers. Messaging channels and knowledge connectors are toggle-only —
// each names a single external service, so there is no organization-specific
// name to respect and indexing their label maps is correct.
//
// The failure mode this guards is drift, not a bug in that code: reading a
// built-in name map directly renders the shipped name, silently ignoring the
// organization's own. That reads correct in review and only shows up for
// deployments that actually renamed something.
//
// So: indexing the built-in label maps is flagged. Use the catalog hook's
// `label(id)` instead — it falls back to the built-in name when no override is
// set, so the shipped behaviour is unchanged.
//
// Legitimate non-label uses are NOT flagged, because they do not index:
//   - `Object.keys(providerDisplayNames)` to enumerate ids
//   - `providerDisplayNames` passed as the fallback inside the catalog itself
// Plugin diagnostics are not suppressible via `biome-ignore`; when a site truly
// must show the shipped name (naming a vendor's own console, say), read it via
// a local alias or a comment-documented constant instead.
language js

`providerDisplayNames[$id]` where {
  register_diagnostic(
    span = $id,
    message = "Use the organization's own name for the provider: `useModelProviderCatalog().label(id)`. Indexing providerDisplayNames renders the shipped name and ignores an admin's rename."
  )
}
